SM(514,{"n":"Romans 8 Continued","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Romans 8 Continued.mp3","d":2157.8,"s":[[0.16,"Come and study Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.08,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed Church, but now an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.92,"But so he continues in verse 12."],[25.68,"Therefore, brethren, we are debtors, not to the flesh, to live according to the flesh."],[31.12,"So what does he mean by debtors?"],[33.12,"Well, our flesh wants all these things."],[35.62,"It craves all these things, it demands all these things."],[38.18,"And what St."],[38.9,"Paul is saying with this debtor language is you don't owe it anything."],[43.8,"You don't have to satisfy those desires."],[47.32,"Just because your flesh wants these things, you don't have to say yes."],[51.12,"You don't have to feed them."],[52.72,"And that means you don't, because we don't owe it anything, because we don't have to feed it, then we don't have to live according to it."],[58.4,"For if you live according to the flesh, you will die"],[62.68,"But if by the Spirit you put to death the deeds of the body, you will live."],[69.72,"So this is pretty pretty clear."],[74.2,"If you get rid of those things and stop following those things, you will live."],[80.52,"If you continue to follow after them, you will die, because that's where that road leads."],[84.36,"Not God's going to get angry at you and he's going to kill you or breaking his rules."],[88.28,"That's just where the. book, the wages of sin is death"],[93.96,"You keep sinning, you earn death."],[96.68,"When you get your paycheck, it's what you've earned."],[99.88,"By what you've done."],[101.24,"So he's saying, not Do do that."],[103.0,"Rather put it to death and live"],[106.88,"And this language here in discussion is the basis of what we call asceticism in the church."],[112.4,"The idea that our flesh desires all of these things."],[118.72,"And that there is a virtue to for a time."],[123.3,"Like during Lent that we just finished, saying, you know what?"],[126.82,"I'm not going to gratify all your desires for food."],[129.62,"I'm not going to gratify all your desires for sleep and comfort."],[133.62,"I'm not going to go and spend all the money I have on things that you know entertain me and make me happy."],[139.78,"I'm going to give some of it, some more of it to those in need."],[142.58,"That denying ourselves in order to foc refocus ourselves on the things of the spirit, that's where this. comes that's where that comes from here"],[150.62,"And again, it's not because any of those things are like food is evil or any of these things are evil."],[158.06,"It's that when we pursue them, when we set our minds on them, when that's our focus, when that's all we're thinking about, that leads us down a road that leads us away from God and to death."],[170.06,"Speaking of reg regarding asceticism, yeah, I I was I was reading through the gospels and um Jesus said that it it is easier for uh it is easier for wealthy for it's easier for a camel to pass through the eye of a needle than for a wealthy man to enter the kingdom of heaven."],[185.82,"Yeah. We have indoor plumbing, yeah, electricity, climate control, food in our discretion, when when we want we want it. it we want the way"],[196.1,"Um we're richer than 99% of the people who have ever lived, just by living in the United States."],[202.42,"In the world today."],[204.18,"In the world today, it's a good 90%."],[206.18,"We live as we live as monarchs."],[207.86,"Yeah. We really do."],[209.62,"So this is especially dangerous for us."],[212.68,"We we think of ourselves most of ourselves are just sort of middle class, not too poor, not too rich, but we're really very, very wealthy."],[220.26,"If if we lived in a slum in Haiti, fasting would not be as important to us."],[225.38,"Because we wouldn't have plenty to eat."],[228.16,"And we wouldn't have plenty to drink, and we wouldn't have money that we're wasting on frivolous things to entertain ourselves."],[234.72,"We wouldn't have any of those things to deny. ourselves"],[238.84,"And so, yes, this is why monasticism emerges after Christianity becomes legal."],[246.6,"Because when Christianity was still an illegal, illicit religion, people didn't really have a choice."],[251.73,"There are all kinds of jobs you couldn't get if you were a Christian."],[255.49,"There were times when you would just be killed."],[258.05,"You'd be killed by the authorities for being a Christian."],[260.85,"And so didn't have a lot of options."],[263.41,"Once Christianity became legal, and then when it became the official religion of the Roman Empire, then it became possible for someone to be a Christian and be wealthy, to be a Christian and be a government official, to be a Christian and do these other things."],[279.09,"And so that's when asceticism became especially important."],[284.09,"And that's when people started saying, you know, I need to get away from this whole system and deny myself the whole thing."],[294.49,"And remove myself from it and started forming monastic communities."],[298.41,"Because every every Christian was an ascetic when it was illegal."],[307.77,"There was no joke."],[308.57,"I mean, everyone who was in your church wanted, truly wanted to be there, ifs I no' mistaken."],[314.47,"And so that's what makes asceticism now especially important, as you're pointing out, for us as modern, wealthy Western people."],[323.27,"It's all the more important for us."],[324.91,"It's we have such a much easier time falling into the mind of the flesh."],[330.85,"Pursuing after these things."],[332.85,"Or thinking, you know, St."],[334.53,"Paul says if you're going down that route, you're at enmity with God."],[338.05,"You can't sort of balance it out."],[339.49,"Like I'm gonna spend, you know, eight hours a day focusing on the things of the flesh, and then when I get home later, then I'll spend an hour praying and focus on the things of the spirit."],[353.09,"You know, I'll balance it out somehow, or I'll spend a couple hours Sunday morning and then the rest of the time I'll be focused on the things of the flesh."],[359.29,"Doesn't work that way."],[360.77,"It doesn't work that way."],[361.73,"You've got to choose one or the other."],[363.33,"And if we're gonna choose to follow the spirit, then with all these temptations around us and stuff, we're gonna have to be very vigilant about not all.owing ourselves to become comfortable and start going down that other road and focusing on the wrong things"],[377.37,"I don't have a question."],[378.57,"Yeah. So whenever it says like sin, the path of sin leads to death."],[383.61,"What is the death referring to?"],[386.17,"It's referring to all kinds of death."],[389.21,"So it's referring to physical death, but also a physical death."],[393.37,"You know, sorry, the spirit who then brings us to resurrection."],[397.87,"And this is a death without resurrection to new life."],[401.87,"So this is condemnation."],[403.15,"This is physical death and spiritual death."],[405.47,"So spiritual death, it means the options of resurrection."],[408.75,"Well, it means it means eternal condemnation."],[411.71,"Yeah. It means what people call hell, even though the word hell doesn't show up in the Bible."],[417.03,"But it means, yeah, it means eternal condemnation."],[420.23,"That's what it's talking about."],[421.27,"That's where that road leads."],[422.47,"Destruction. It's the way Proverbs puts it."],[424.79,"There's a way that seems right to a man, and its end is destruction."],[428.79,"Yeah, and that's trying to warn us off."],[431.27,"Because as that says, the way, see, this road, it looks good to us."],[435.91,"Wealth looks good to us, pleasure looks good to us."],[439.03,"Alright, being admired looks good to us."],[441.19,"Gratifying all our desires looks good to us."],[443.51,"And so it's a warning that okay, yeah, this part of the road that you're starting out on looks really good."],[450.87,"But here's where it leads."],[452.47,"And that's destruction."],[453.91,"That's death. That's condemnation."],[456.31,"Remember, chapter 8 started with there's no condemnation now for us who walk according to the Spirit."],[460.15,"Because all of us were on that road at one point"],[465.47,"There's nobody who wasn't on that road except Christ."],[468.83,"All of us have been on that road at some point, but now we've been set free from it to go in a different direction."],[474.75,"It leads to life."],[477.15,"In terms of uh you mentioned something about Lent."],[480.51,"So do you think we're supposed to, or whatever we do doing Lent, we're supposed to be doing that also outside Lent?"],[488.19,"Yeah, Lent, it's more intense."],[490.51,"It's more intense during Lent."],[492.43,"But it's sort of like boot camp with the military."],[495.15,"You go to boot camp, you're there for this short, relatively short period of time, and everything's super intense, you know, for for that time."],[503.79,"And then when you get out, you're in the military, you're not supposed to sort of forget all of it."],[505.15,"But it's not that intense"],[507.05,"And sort of walk away."],[511.29,"You're supposed to keep what you've learned and keep it up."],[514.41,"So, for example, once once we're done after ascension, we'll start fasting on Wednesdays and Fridays again."],[521.37,"We don't fast every day like we do during Lent, super strictly, but a couple days a week."],[526.41,"So we continue to do that."],[527.85,"It's just not it's sort of like boot camp when we get to Lent."],[531.77,"And there's also a case to be made for fasting, not just dietary fasting, but fasting from all sorts of things."],[538.81,"Oh, yeah. Yeah."],[540.25,"Just dietary fasting."],[541.45,"Yeah. A lot of people I know, and I think it's a very good idea."],[545.61,"Like get off social media and stuff during Lent."],[548.49,"And just say, you know what, I'm going to take a little period of time and not"],[548.85,"The sensors die."],[550.21,"Yeah, and all that kind of stuff."],[555.49,"Like I meant with boot camp, you learn things."],[557.89,"Yeah. You learn things about yourself, you learn things."],[560.14,"And that's what's supposed to happen during Lent."],[562.3,"By being very disciplined for the short period of time, we learn all kinds of things about ourselves."],[566.38,"Technically, there are some days when you can have alcohol during Lent, but I always advise people not to have any."],[571.18,"Because if you can't go 50 days without having an alcoholic drink, that says something."],[576.08,"About your relationship to alcohol."],[577.6,"If you can't quit for 50, it means you have some kind of unhealthy thing going on."],[582.4,"And if if you can't get off your phone right at social media for 50 days, there's probably something unhealthy going on there."],[593.36,"Turn off the TV, readable things."],[594.0,"Yeah I mean, if if there's something you can't stop for 50 days, then there's some kind of problem going on with your relationship with it."],[605.96,"They're all in trouble."],[607.32,"Yeah. Well, no, we all that's why we all do Lent."],[610.44,"There's nobody who's like, oh, I don't need to bother with it because I've got it all together."],[617.62,"Well, you can look at the once we're done with the ascension is like preparing for the next Lent."],[624.4,"Well, yeah. And well, and that's that's what I tell people a lot of times in in confession is that all the places when you look at Lent, if you go to Lent and you try to keep all the disciplines, and you look at all the places where you fail, because we all fail, you look all the places. where you fail, you say, okay, now I know these are the things I need to work on for the next year"],[643.8,"And then when the next Lent comes around, you do another checkup."],[647.78,"See where you stand."],[648.66,"And maybe you do better with some of those, maybe you do worse with some of those."],[652.18,"Maybe you do and then that sets for the next year."],[654.66,"Okay, now I know what I need to work on."],[656.82,"And we all just keep working and you know, trying to do better."],[660.34,"Because again, it's a road, it's not it's a it's a walk the way we live our whole life."],[665.54,"I think right, continuing down that road."],[667.86,"Wildly underestimated the the intensity of the Lenten season."],[673.46,"And uh I made plans and things like that and uh and trying to keep up with the singing, learning the new music, the praying, the and I look back and I said, What was I thinking when I agreed to this kind of thing?"],[685.42,"And it was like I should I really should be cutting all of this out, making space."],[690.3,"So I mean, yes, next length."],[692.54,"I'm making more space."],[694.54,"Yeah. Yeah. And so that's the goal is that we're continuing to progress and draw closer to Christ."],[701.26,"Because none of us are there yet."],[702.54,"We're all somewhere on the way."],[705.1,"What's important is that we're moving in the right direction."],[707.82,"So verse 14."],[710.3,"For as many as are led by the Spirit of God, these are sons of God."],[715.26,"For you did not receive the spirit of bondage again to fear, but you received the spirit of adoption, by whom we cry out, Abba Father."],[723.98,"Spirit himself bears witness with our spirit that we are children of God, and if children, then heirs, heirs of God and joint heirs with Christ."],[732.42,"If indeed we suffer with him, that we may also be glorified together."],[737.06,"So he starts out as many as are led by the Spirit of God, these are sons of God."],[742.66,"Now you notice it changes, the language here that changes from sons of God to children of God is actually the language in the Greek."],[750.26,"He says sons of God first here in verse 14, and then he says children of God later."],[754.74,"And so when he says sons of God here in verse 14, that's significant."],[759.46,"Because sons of God is a title in the Old Testament for a certain group of what we would call angels."],[768.58,"They actually sort of outrank angels."],[771.06,"These are the end the angelic. beings who stand in God's presence all the time"],[778.78,"So when St."],[780.94,"Paul says that those who follow the Spirit, or in this case are led by the Spirit, are sons of God, and refers to the Spirit as the spirit of adoption."],[791.19,"This is what he's talking about."],[792.71,"He's not just talking about, well, God loves us the way he loves kids."],[796.71,"He means no longer are we, remember the flesh, or again cast out of paradise and having this mortal flesh."],[803.35,"In paradise, Adam and Eve were in the presence of God."],[806.73,"Because that's what paradise is."],[807.93,"It's where God is."],[808.89,"It's a place where God dwells."],[810.65,"They were there in his presence, they lived with him, they were part of this family with him, with the angels."],[816.73,"God would come and walk in the garden with them"],[823.87,"And so this is what St."],[825.15,"Paul is saying."],[826.43,"That those who are led by the Spirit, those who follow this path that leads to life, that's where this path leads."],[835.63,"It leads to us becoming what we were created to be originally."],[842.83,"To becoming these members of these members of God's family."],[849.87,"Well, okay, so they're making that comparison, the sons of God and that pathway for us to take."],[858.09,"And so this is why he talks about children of God."],[862.14,"That means we're heirs, heirs of God and joint heirs with Christ."],[868.24,"So Christ, as he's going to say, he's going to refer to Christ being the firstborn among many brethren."],[877.44,"But Christ obviously is the only begotten son of God."],[881.92,"But firstborn in terms of heirs."],[884.9,"The way inheritance worked in this culture is that all of the children inherited through the firstborn."],[891.94,"Technically speaking, whoever the firstborn son was inherited everything."],[896.02,"But it was then his duty to then distribute that to the other heirs."],[901.5,"Distributed to the other heirs."],[902.9,"And so there's a point in uh St."],[904.86,"Matthew's gospel where somebody comes to Jesus and says, uh, Master, tell my brother to divide the inheritance with me, because apparently his brother was the firstborn and had inherited everything and didn't give him anything."],[917.36,"And so he comes to Jesus to ask Jesus, you know, hey, you're a rabbi, you come tell him to give me my share."],[923.86,"And Christ tells him, You shouldn't be worried about that."],[926.98,"Why don't you come follow me and not worry about the inheritance?"],[931.3,"And so the same kind of idea is here."],[933.31,"Christ is the firstborn, not because he came into existence at some point, but he's the he has this status."],[938.75,"The only begotten Son of God is the firstborn of God"],[941.95,"So he everything that belongs to the Father belongs to Christ."],[945.39,"And it's through Christ that, then all of those blessings and all of those things are distributed to us when we're adopted as God's children through the Spirit."],[954.87,"And so Christ, at his return, is going to inherit everything."],[959.35,"The whole world and everything in it, the whole creation, is his inheritance."],[965.27,"And so St."],[966.23,"Paul is talking about him sharing that with us."],[968.87,"And this is this is the language he uses."],[970.95,"Remember when Christ tells his disciples, you'll sit on twelve thrones and judge the twelve tribes of Israel."],[976.39,"This language that they're gonna and Saint Paul's gonna say in First Corinthians, don't you know that we'll judge angels?"],[981.09,"This idea of God sharing his Christ sharing his creation, his dominion with us."],[987.97,"So what St."],[988.77,"Paul is describing here is what the church calls theosis. sometimes called in in Western terminology, deification"],[995.93,"That we were created to become what Christ in his human nature is by nature, his humanity, which has been united to God."],[1005.05,"We become a part of sort of God's council."],[1008.33,"This is imagery that's used throughout the Old Testament."],[1010.57,"God is the king."],[1011.71,"Now Christ sits on his throne, Christ is enthroned at the right hand of God, and he has this council."],[1016.69,"His advisors, his officials, around him that are portrayed as angels in the Old Testament."],[1022.87,"There's God in this angelic council."],[1025.19,"And so what Saint Paul is talking about here is about us, we as human beings, through the Holy Spirit, through what Christ has done, who those of us who follow after the Spirit, that's where it leads."],[1034.95,"s. But it' a royal family"],[1035.31,"We become a part of not just God's family."],[1040.08,"We become part of this royal family over the whole, over the whole creation, that we're transformed into the image of Christ."],[1048.08,"And that's what he means there at the end."],[1050.48,"If indeed we suffer with him, that we may also be glorified together."],[1054.24,"This is Christ's glorification."],[1056.22,"His enthronement, his ruling over the whole creation."],[1059.1,"And so Saint Paul is here introducing the idea of suffering."],[1062.14,"He's about to expand on that in the next few verses."],[1064.8,"Remember, Christ suffered."],[1066.72,"He suffered, he died, and then was glorified."],[1069.6,"And so St."],[1070.24,"Paul is here introducing the idea: yes, we're going down that same path that leads to glory, that leads to being a part of this royal family. of God, ruling over the whole creation"],[1082.12,"But the path that leads there, just like Christ's path leads us through suffering in this world."],[1088.04,"So so what about uh the levels of the ecosystem?"],[1092.76,"I mean, what happens?"],[1094.04,"I mean, like if somebody's just halfway through and they've improved so much, but they still have so much to, and they die in the well that's everyone."],[1103.08,"There is no there is no perfect."],[1104.84,"But then you have God's presence and in this."],[1107.88,"And we continue to grow."],[1110.36,"We continue to grow."],[1112.12,"Yeah. If it begins in this life."],[1114.76,"disru And it gets. within thepted"],[1117.32,"I mean, if you're not that perfect, I mean you could mess things up."],[1120.2,"There is no perfect."],[1121.72,"The distance between us and God is infinite."],[1124.04,"We're never gonna get to a point where it's where I know everything Christ knows"],[1130.14,"Or I'm perfect the way Christ is perfect."],[1132.62,"That will never happen."],[1133.82,"I can continue to grow for eternity."],[1137.42,"But I mean the structure of heaven and the order of heaven will be disrupted."],[1142.06,"Well, I mean, we may end up doing another rebellion just like Satan did."],[1145.82,"I mean, go through."],[1146.78,"No, because there won't be any sin."],[1150.54,"But if we're not perfect, we're all gonna be sinning."],[1154.54,"No. Then just have stages of mortification"],[1159.34,"Yeah. Adam wasn't sinful when he was created, but he wasn't perfect either."],[1165.02,"He was like a child."],[1167.47,"He wasn't mature."],[1168.03,"He only existed for a couple days"],[1170.31,"He'd only been alive for a couple days."],[1175.24,"He may have had an adult body, but I mean he'd so we all grow and can and continue to grow."],[1180.84,"So it's not it's not just sin."],[1183.48,"Yeah, sin is sin is is uh it's like disease."],[1188.68,"But you can be completely free from disease and completely healthy, that doesn't mean you're full grown and mature."],[1195.64,"Those aren't the same thing."],[1197.24,"We're just imperfect."],[1199.46,"There is no."],[1200.94,"If we talk about perfect, we're talking about Christ."],[1204.66,"We will never be perfect."],[1206.9,"We'll never be identical to Christ."],[1209.86,"We can become more and more like Christ for eternity."],[1213.74,"We will continue to grow and continue to learn and continue to glorify God."],[1220.54,"Forever. So this is this is progress that goes on forever."],[1224.62,"We never reach a point where we're like, okay, we're done."],[1227.66,"So God takes us where we are, and we grow, and that growth begins in this life and then continues into eternity."],[1233.82,"So it never stops."],[1236.38,"Never stops. Sinning stops."],[1239.42,"Sin stops. When this world is transformed, sin stops, death stops."],[1246.0,"Those things Christ puts an end to."],[1248.8,"But our growth and our maturing and our growth and understanding and all of those things continue, continue forever."],[1256.52,"I guess one of the things Because God's infinite."],[1259.24,"This idea that we're we're we're not perfect, we're not perfect, we will continue to grow, and sin will be will be vanquished in heaven, which means that there was a time when sin was permitted amongst the angels themselves through free will."],[1276.12,"Is that correct?"],[1277.08,"So there was a time when the angels, the angels remained immortal, which means they couldn't repent."],[1284.12,"I'll be more specific."],[1285.16,"In Genesis 3, when God casts them out of the garden, the reason God casts them out of the garden, the reason God cast them out of paradise is he says, if we don't, they'll eat from the tree of life and they'll live forever in this sinful state."],[1300.92,"Like demons. Meaning we would have been like demons"],[1304.96,"And everyone that had come after them if we had remained immortal and sinful."],[1310.0,"Okay. We would be like the demons."],[1312.48,"And so God cast humanity out, gave them mortal bodies as a mercy to it and gave us this life in this world so that we could repent."],[1323.84,"And then so that we could be, so that we could be purified from sin."],[1327.92,"But it's I guess my question specifically is I guess the state of heaven was in a different state at the time of the rebellion?"],[1337.04,"Or there was a different time?"],[1338.96,"Or is that a mystery of the church that is undefined?"],[1341.28,"Okay, okay. You're you're you've you you're talking about the idea that the angels rebelled sometime before the world was created."],[1346.48,"that Is what you're thinking?"],[1346.64,"Okay Yes. That's John Milton."],[1354.44,"That's not the Bible or the Church Fathers."],[1357.0,"So there are, and we'll get into this more when we loop around and get into Genesis."],[1364.52,"But there there were three and there are three angelic rebellions in the Bible."],[1369.8,"One is just the devil, and that's in Genesis 3."],[1374.92,"Okay. One happens in uh Genesis 6, really 5 and 6, and one happens in Genesis chapter 11."],[1383.72,"Okay. So, but we'll we'll get into that more when we loop around."],[1388.46,"Another thing I thought I understood is now been turned on its head."],[1391.78,"Okay. And in all three cases, human beings participated in that angelic rebellion."],[1399.28,"Okay. Yeah. We're led by them into rebellion."],[1402.8,"And that that's part of what's in the background here with the idea of sinful flesh and following it."],[1408.16,"And then following the spirit."],[1410.24,"Okay. Are things perfect?"],[1414.08,"It depends on what you mean by perfect."],[1416.32,"If you mean do they still sin, then no."],[1419.36,"If by perfect you mean they're not still growing, then they're not perfect in that sense."],[1425.2,"And being created beings, they're not omniscient or omnipotent."],[1428.65,"Okay. They're continuing to grow closer."],[1432.09,"Now they're way ahead of me."],[1435.07,"In terms of closeness to God."],[1437.07,"But there's never a point where you exhaust God, where you totally comprehend God and you know everything God knows, and you see everything really God sees."],[1448.19,"We can continue forever."],[1449.63,"It takes eternity to cross an infinite distance at any speed."],[1456.59,"There's some interesting questions for some of the ancient fathers."],[1462.43,"So he continues to talk about suffering."],[1464.67,"Verse 18 for I consider that the sufferings of this present time are not worthy to be compared with the glory which shall be revealed in us."],[1473.07,"So the glory that will be revealed in us, he's talking again about this transformation."],[1479.91,"He's talking about theosis."],[1481.19,"He's talking talking about us being adopted into this failure."],[1485.83,"So how did these people in Rome not even understand him?"],[1488.87,"I mean, they were not theologians and they did not have your understanding."],[1492.79,"And he talks in such language."],[1495.03,"It was a hard language."],[1496.87,"It was it was easier for them."],[1499.03,"Because the things I'm bringing out and talking about are things that the the Jewish literature, especially at the time, and even some of the pagan literature talked about all the time."],[1509.11,"So he was speaking their language."],[1510.79,"They would understand"],[1511.99,"We live 2,000 years later."],[1514.15,"So I've got to sort of do all this bringing in these things."],[1518.23,"Like I was talking about the Epistle of Barnabas before and the Day of Atonement ritual."],[1522.31,"Well, they'd seen the Day of Atonement ritual."],[1523.03,"the Day of Atonement ritual. Paul can just refer to it and they're like, oh yeah."],[1525.15,"They knew what that was about."],[1526.83,"St. But I haven't seen it."],[1534.27,"I have to go and do research and find out about it because of when I live."],[1538.91,"So yeah, that for them, for that, no, I'm not saying, you know, St."],[1543.63,"Peter's gonna say later in one of his epistles that that St."],[1546.99,"Paul says many things that are hard to understand."],[1550.35,"So I'm not saying this was like super easy elementary stuff."],[1554.61,"This was this was serious stuff, but it wasn't beyond their understanding because they were used to talking in these terms."],[1561.65,"So when he refers to the sons of God, they would have been thinking of angels."],[1566.61,"They would have been thinking of, you know, when he mentions, you know, our mortal bodies, they would have oh right, they would have made these connections because this was the language they were used to hearing at the synagogue and when they talked about religious things."],[1580.81,"Sort of in the same way that if I if I make a reference, like if I talk about you you know, you remember on Posca when I knocked on the door and I said, Lift up your heads, O ye gates."],[1592.33,"Now what if I went down the road to a Protestant church and I said, You know how on Posca we knock on the doors that we s they'd look at me like, What are you talking about?"],[1603.95,"They'd have no clue."],[1604.91,"And I'd have to go back and explain."],[1606.19,"I'd have to say, Well, okay, Pasca is sort of like what you call Easter, and we go and we do the words from Psalm 24 and we beg at the right."],[1615.91,"I'd have to explain it all to them."],[1617.59,"But you just understand because you've been there."],[1619.83,"It's the same kind of thing here."],[1621.11,"Say Paul says it to them, and they just sort of understand because he and they live in this same kind of environment."],[1628.23,"But for us, it's like, what?"],[1631.91,"We have to, we need a little more explanation."],[1634.87,"So the glory that's going to be written, this destiny that we have in Christ."],[1638.63,"He says, if you compare all the things we have to go through in this life, all the sufferings we have to go through."],[1644.31,"And he's talking to people who have suffered."],[1645.83,"Remember, a lot of them have just gotten thrown out of their homes for a year because the emperor got mad at the Jews."],[1651.97,"And Christians are being persecuted in these things."],[1654.29,"So this is legit suffering."],[1655.65,"This isn't like, oh, I dropped my Starbucks."],[1661.21,"These are not first world problems they're having."],[1665.66,"But he says, even those legitimate sufferings."],[1668.08,"If you compare those to this destiny we have in Christ, it's nothing."],[1672.8,"For the earnest expectation of the creation eagerly waits for the revealing of the sons of God."],[1679.12,"So he says it isn't just us, the whole creation is waiting for the day."],[1686.16,"Waiting for the day of Christ's return, when the sons of God are revealed, when we receive this destiny."],[1692.16,"Why? Because the whole creation is going to be purified and transformed."],[1695.92,"The world, the animals, the plants."],[1698.62,"Everything in creation is waiting for this day."],[1702.06,"Because remember what happens in Genesis 3."],[1706.18,"God says to Adam, Cursed is the ground, cursed is the earth, because of you."],[1711.86,"Because God had given human beings dominion over the creation."],[1715.62,"And so when we sin, it affects the world around us and the creation."],[1721.86,"It's destructive to the whole creation."],[1724.5,"So the whole creation is waiting for this day, St."],[1727.38,"Paul says. For the creation was subjected to futility in Genesis 3, not willingly, but because of him who subjected it in hope."],[1736.96,"Why in hope?"],[1738.24,"Because part of that, remember, was that human beings were given mortal flesh and were sent out so that they could repent."],[1746.13,"So they could be restored."],[1748.61,"Because the creation itself also will be delivered from the bondage of corruption into the glorious liberty of the children of God."],[1757.17,"So creation itself is going to be freed."],[1760.53,"It's going to be freed of bondage to corruption, to the effects, that taint, that leftover taint of our sin and our wickedness."],[1769.49,"For we know that the whole creation groans and labors with birth pangs together until now."],[1774.53,"Not only that, but we also who have the first fruits of the Spirit, even we ourselves groan within ourselves, eagerly waiting for the adoption, the redemption of our body."],[1784.37,"So we have, he calls here the spirit who we've received the first fruits."],[1787.98,"What were the first fruits?"],[1789.5,"Well, it's when you plant all your crops, the first thing that grows up."],[1793.7,"And that was sort of the guarantee."],[1795.78,"When you saw that first growth, you knew, okay, the crop is coming."],[1801.94,"I planted things correctly."],[1803.22,"It didn't die in the freeze in the winter."],[1805.92,"Things are gonna be okay."],[1807.04,"So now that we have the spirit."],[1808.66,"That's the beginning of our transformation."],[1812.18,"Us beginning to walk after the spirit now is the beginning of this path that leads to our destiny."],[1818.1,"And it's the guarantee of that destiny that we've already that we've already received."],[1824.82,"And so, since we've received that, we like the creation are eager for that day."],[1830.66,"And Christ will return when the world will be restored."],[1833.62,"And when, as it says, our our b bododiesies, no, it's not flesh again, body will be redeemed."],[1835.38,"For we were saved in this hope"],[1841.58,"But hope that is seen is not hope."],[1843.98,"For why does one still hope for what he sees?"],[1847.74,"So we're saved."],[1853.58,"We're saved from the power of sin and death for this hope."],[1857.34,"It's not like, oh, okay, I got saved, so now I'm good."],[1860.06,"I'm not going to hell."],[1861.66,"Now I go and do whatever I want, I guess."],[1864.38,"Try not to sin too much."],[1866.86,"It's not how it is."],[1867.9,"We're saved for this hope."],[1868.94,"We're saved for the power of sin and death, so that now we're free to follow the Spirit."],[1873.5,"So that we're free now to go down this path that leads here."],[1877.9,"And then, of course, he says, you know, why does one still hope for what one sees?"],[1882.98,"You don't sit there with the Amazon package in your hand saying, Bat boy, I hope my package shows up today."],[1889.2,"You've already got it."],[1890.62,"So that's what that's what St."],[1892.22,"Paul is saying."],[1892.86,"You don't hope for what you already have."],[1894.38,"So yeah, we haven't we haven't achieved this destiny yet."],[1898.22,"But if we hope for what we do not see, we eagerly wait for it with perseverance."],[1905.18,"Likewise, the spirit also helps in our weaknesses, for we do not know what we should pray for as we ought."],[1911.74,"But the spirit Hsimelf makes intercession for us with groanings which cannot be uttered."],[1917.26,"Now he who searches the hearts knows what the mind of the Spirit is, because he makes intercession for the saints according to the will of God."],[1926.34,"So St. Paul's saying we don't even really know what we should pray for."],[1930.98,"Why? Well, what are the things we tend to pray for?"],[1934.26,"Things we tend to pray for are usually things that are according to the mind of the flesh."],[1940.1,"That's, you know, God help me get this promotion."],[1943.46,"You know, God help me pass this test I didn't study for."],[1946.02,"Not you, of course."],[1949.38,"You know, that's God, you know, let me win the lottery."],[1953.63,"Whatever. Most of the things that we pray, we're not even praying for the right things."],[1958.21,"Well, no, that's a good thing."],[1959.97,"Depending on what you do with it."],[1962.15,"And if you're grateful for it when you have it."],[1964.55,"I mean, I've I've when I get sick, I tend to very quickly pray that God would make me better."],[1968.55,"But when I'm when I'm healthy, I don't often pray and thank God for the fact that I'm healthy"],[1974.59,"You know, that's but you know, we we don't even know what we should pray for."],[1978.59,"But as he says, the Holy Spirit obviously knows his own mind."],[1982.61,"He was contrasting the mind of the flesh and the mind of the spirit."],[1985.35,"And so the Spirit comes in and intercedes for us."],[1989.11,"He sort of the the image is that the Holy Spirit is sort of translating to God the Father first."],[1996.55,"Whatever it is that we're saying."],[1998.16,"The Holy Spirit sort of translates it into the things that we really need."],[2003.6,"You know, the uh uh this the head of the Coptic Church is Sh Schnnogodera, of Schnod.er"],[2010.8,"Yeah. He passed away. but yeah, I know you're talking about that"],[2014.6,"I listened to them listen to some of his speeches and stuff, and uh you know, mostly what I could understand from what he says we pray for are really the fruits of the spirit."],[2024.94,"So we really pray to be meek, we pray to be loved, we pray to be joyful, and those are guaranteed."],[2031.1,"Like if you pray hard enough, you can be sure you're gonna come out catching that."],[2035.42,"You know, you have to stick stick with it and and like when you say you pray you're gonna get what you pray for."],[2041.5,"These things if you really pray hard for knowledge and you mean it and you stick with it and you persevere, you're guaranteed to get it."],[2048.54,"Yeah. Well that's uh that's what Christ tells, wherever he says, Don't worry about what you'll eat and what you'll wear and all these things, he says, seek first the kingdom of God and his righteousness, and then all these other things will be taken care of."],[2063.32,"You won't have to worry about those things."],[2065.46,"Yeah, and then it's and and St."],[2067.38,"Paul says at one point if anyone lacks wisdom, let him ask God, who gives generously to everyone."],[2073.32,"Yeah, if those are the things that we're asking for."],[2075.8,"Yeah. But even when we're asking for the wrong things, it says here the Holy Spirit will sort of translate for us for the things that we actually need, you know, even if we don't always understand what we really need."],[2087.72,"Um, but yeah, those are the things that we really need."],[2090.6,"Back in my Protestant days, there were warnings you shouldn't pray for patience."],[2094.4,"Because you'll get it, yeah."],[2096.68,"You'll be tested."],[2098.2,"Well, yeah, it's again and again and again until you get patience."],[2099.96,"Yeah, Saint St"],[2104.56,"Augustine said when he was a young man, he used to pray, Lord, give me chastity, but not yet."],[2113.2,"So yeah. But yeah, those are the things."],[2120.32,"So this is probably a good place, even though we're not at the end of the chapter."],[2124.48,"And this is probably a good place to leave off, because as we as we go on now, we're going to get into predestination and stuff."],[2130.24,"And so that probably requires its own its own discussion."],[2133.76,"So thank you, everybody."],[2135.52,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2142.8,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecouncil at ancientfaith.com."],[2144.72,"whole. That'scouncil at ancientfaithcom."]],"o":[{"t":21.92,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 8:12-13 - Debtors, not to the flesh","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verse 12</b>: we are <b>debtors</b>, not to the flesh</li><li class=\"d1\">flesh craves, demands - you <b>don't owe it anything</b></li><li class=\"d1\">don't have to say yes, don't have to feed it → don't have to live by it</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verse 13</b>: live by flesh = <b>die</b>; by Spirit put to death deeds of body = <b>live</b></li><li class=\"d1\">clear: stop following those things → live; continue → die</li><li class=\"d1\">not God angry and killing you or breaking his rules</li><li class=\"d1\">\"wages of sin is death\" - keep sinning, <b>you earn death</b>, like a paycheck</li><li class=\"d0\">Put it to death and live</li></ul>"},{"t":106.88,"lv":3,"h":"Asceticism","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Basis of <b>asceticism</b> in the church</li><li class=\"d0\">Flesh desires everything; virtue in saying <b>no for a time</b></li><li class=\"d1\">like <b>Lent</b> just finished</li><li class=\"d1\">not gratifying desires for food, sleep, comfort, spending on entertainment</li><li class=\"d1\">give more to those in need</li><li class=\"d0\">Denying ourselves to <b>refocus on the things of the Spirit</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not that food etc. is <b>evil</b></li><li class=\"d1\">problem = when we <b>set our minds on them</b>, all we think about → road away from God, to death</li></ul>"},{"t":170.06,"lv":2,"h":"Q&amp;A: wealth and asceticism","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: camel through eye of a needle - we have plumbing, electricity, climate control, food on demand</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Richer than 99%</b> of people who ever lived, just in the US - \"we live as monarchs\"</li><li class=\"d1\">we think we're middle class; really <b>very, very wealthy</b></li><li class=\"d1\">slum in Haiti: fasting wouldn't matter - nothing to deny</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Monasticism</b> emerges after Christianity becomes legal</li><li class=\"d1\">while illegal: jobs closed to you, sometimes <b>killed</b> - no choice, <b>every Christian an ascetic</b></li><li class=\"d1\">once legal / official religion: could be Christian and wealthy, official, etc.</li><li class=\"d1\">people then left \"the whole system\" → monastic communities</li><li class=\"d0\">Asceticism <b>more</b> important for modern wealthy Westerners</li><li class=\"d1\">easier to fall into <b>mind of the flesh</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Enmity with God</b> - can't balance: 8 hours flesh, 1 hour prayer, or Sunday morning only</li><li class=\"d1\">\"doesn't work that way\" - choose one or the other</li><li class=\"d1\">must be <b>vigilant</b> not to get comfortable</li></ul>"},{"t":377.37,"lv":2,"h":"Q&amp;A: what is the \"death\"?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: what does the path of sin leading to death refer to?</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>All kinds of death</b>: physical death, spiritual death</li><li class=\"d1\">death <b>without resurrection</b> to new life = <b>condemnation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"what people call hell, even though the word hell doesn't show up in the Bible\"</li><li class=\"d1\">= <b>eternal condemnation</b>, destruction</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Proverbs</b>: a way that seems right to a man, its end is destruction</li><li class=\"d0\">Road <b>looks good</b>: wealth, pleasure, being admired, gratifying desires</li><li class=\"d1\">warning: starts well, <b>here's where it leads</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Ch. 8 began: <b>no condemnation</b> for those who walk by the Spirit</li><li class=\"d1\">all of us were on that road - <b>except Christ</b>; now set free to go another direction → life</li></ul>"},{"t":477.15,"lv":2,"h":"Q&amp;A: Lent and beyond Lent","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: should we do Lent-type discipline outside Lent?</li><li class=\"d0\">Lent = <b>more intense</b>; like <b>boot camp</b></li><li class=\"d1\">short, super intense - then you keep what you learned</li><li class=\"d1\">after Ascension: fasting <b>Wednesdays and Fridays</b> again, not every day strictly</li><li class=\"d0\">Fast from more than diet: <b>social media</b>, TV</li><li class=\"d1\">learn things about yourself in boot camp</li><li class=\"d0\">Alcohol technically allowed some Lenten days - he advises <b>none</b></li><li class=\"d1\">can't go 50 days without it → says something about <b>your relationship to it</b></li><li class=\"d1\">same for phone / social media: \"something unhealthy going on\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Everyone does Lent - \"nobody who's got it all together\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Confession</b>: Lent = checkup</li><li class=\"d1\">see where you fail → <b>what to work on</b> for the year; next Lent, another checkup</li><li class=\"d1\">it's a <b>road, a walk</b> the whole of life</li><li class=\"d0\">Goal: keep progressing, draw closer to Christ - \"none of us are there yet\"; <b>direction</b> matters</li></ul>"},{"t":707.82,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 8:14-17 - Sons of God, heirs with Christ","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verse 14</b>: led by the Spirit = <b>sons of God</b>; spirit of <b>adoption</b>, \"Abba, Father\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Spirit bears witness we are <b>children</b>, heirs, <b>joint heirs with Christ</b> - if we suffer with him, glorified together</li><li class=\"d0\">Greek shifts: <b>sons</b> of God (v.14) → <b>children</b> (v.16)</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Sons of God\" in OT = title for a group of <b>angels</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"outrank angels\" - the beings who <b>stand in God's presence</b> all the time</li><li class=\"d1\">adoption not just \"God loves us like kids\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Reverses expulsion from <b>paradise</b></li><li class=\"d1\">paradise = where God is; Adam and Eve lived in his presence, <b>part of the family</b> with the angels</li><li class=\"d1\">God walked in the garden with them</li><li class=\"d0\">Path of the Spirit → becoming <b>what we were created to be</b>, members of God's family</li></ul>"},{"t":858.09,"lv":2,"h":"Heirs: Christ the firstborn","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Children → <b>heirs</b> of God, joint heirs with Christ</li><li class=\"d0\">Christ = <b>firstborn among many brethren</b> (coming in v.29); only-begotten Son</li><li class=\"d0\">Inheritance in that culture: all inherit <b>through the firstborn</b></li><li class=\"d1\">firstborn technically got everything, but duty to <b>distribute</b> to other heirs</li><li class=\"d1\">gospel story: man asks Jesus to tell brother to divide the inheritance → \"come follow me, don't worry about it\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Christ firstborn not because he came into existence - <b>status</b></li><li class=\"d1\">all the Father's belongs to Christ → blessings <b>distributed to us</b> when adopted through the Spirit</li><li class=\"d0\">At his return Christ inherits <b>the whole creation</b>; Paul talks of <b>sharing it with us</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>twelve thrones</b> judging the tribes of Israel</li><li class=\"d1\">1 Corinthians: \"don't you know we'll <b>judge angels</b>?\"</li></ul>"},{"t":987.97,"lv":3,"h":"Theosis: God's council and royal family","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">What Paul describes = <b>theosis</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Western term: <b>deification</b></li><li class=\"d0\">We were created to become what <b>Christ in his human nature is by nature</b> - humanity united to God</li><li class=\"d0\">Become part of <b>God's council</b> - OT imagery throughout</li><li class=\"d1\">God the king; Christ enthroned at his right hand</li><li class=\"d1\">advisors, officials around him = <b>angels</b> in OT</li><li class=\"d0\">We, as human beings, through the Spirit and what Christ did, join that</li><li class=\"d1\">not just God's family but a <b>royal family</b> over the whole creation</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>transformed into the image of Christ</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1059.1,"lv":3,"h":"Suffering with him","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">End of v.17: <b>if indeed we suffer with him</b>, that we may be glorified together</li><li class=\"d0\">Glorification = Christ's <b>enthronement</b>, ruling over all creation</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul <b>introduces suffering</b>, expands in next verses</li><li class=\"d0\">Christ suffered, died, <b>then</b> glorified</li><li class=\"d1\">we go down the <b>same path</b> to glory</li><li class=\"d1\">path runs <b>through suffering</b> in this world</li></ul>"},{"t":1088.04,"lv":2,"h":"Q&amp;A: growth, perfection and the saints","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: what if someone's only halfway through improving when they die?</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>No perfect</b> - distance between us and God is <b>infinite</b></li><li class=\"d1\">never know everything Christ knows, never perfect as he is</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>grow for eternity</b>; growth begins in this life, continues</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: would imperfect people disrupt heaven / rebel like Satan?</li><li class=\"d1\">no - <b>no sin</b> there</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Adam</b> not sinful at creation but not perfect</li><li class=\"d1\">\"like a child,\" only alive a couple days; adult body, not mature</li><li class=\"d0\">Sin = like <b>disease</b>; free from disease ≠ full-grown, mature</li><li class=\"d0\">\"If we talk about perfect, we're talking about Christ\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>sin stops, death stops</b> when world transformed</li><li class=\"d1\">growth, maturing, understanding continue <b>forever</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1256.52,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: angelic rebellions","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: angels sinned through free will - was heaven in a different state then?</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Genesis 3</b>: God expels humans so they don't eat of the <b>tree of life</b> and live forever in sinful state</li><li class=\"d1\">immortal and sinful = \"like demons\" - mortal bodies a <b>mercy</b>, to repent and be purified</li><li class=\"d0\">Angels rebelling before creation = <b>John Milton</b>, not the Bible or fathers</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Three angelic rebellions</b> in the Bible</li><li class=\"d1\">devil in <b>Genesis 3</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Genesis 5-6</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Genesis 11</b></li><li class=\"d1\">will return when looping around to Genesis</li><li class=\"d0\">In all three, <b>humans participated</b>, led into rebellion</li><li class=\"d1\">background of \"sinful flesh\" vs following the Spirit</li><li class=\"d0\">Angels \"perfect\"? Don't sin, but not omniscient or omnipotent - <b>still growing</b></li><li class=\"d1\">never exhaust God: \"takes eternity to cross an infinite distance at any speed\"</li></ul>"},{"t":1462.43,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 8:18 - Sufferings vs glory","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verse 18</b>: sufferings of this present time not worthy to be compared with the <b>glory revealed in us</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Glory = transformation, <b>theosis</b>, adoption into the royal family</li><li class=\"d0\">Sufferings of this present time <b>not worthy to be compared</b> to it</li><li class=\"d1\">glory <b>revealed in us</b> = transformation, being adopted into this family</li></ul>"},{"t":1485.83,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: how did the Romans understand this?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: Roman Christians weren't theologians - how did they follow such language?</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Easier for them</b>: Jewish literature (and some pagan) used these themes constantly</li><li class=\"d1\">\"speaking their language\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Us 2,000 years later: must research</li><li class=\"d1\">e.g. <b>Day of Atonement</b> ritual (<i>Epistle of Barnabas</i>) - they'd seen it, Paul just refers to it</li><li class=\"d0\">Peter: Paul says <b>things hard to understand</b> - serious stuff, but not beyond them</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Sons of God\" → they'd think <b>angels</b>; mortal bodies - they'd connect it</li><li class=\"d0\">Analogy: <b>Pascha</b> knocking on doors, \"Lift up your heads, O ye gates\" (Psalm 24)</li><li class=\"d1\">Protestants wouldn't know it; <b>you understand because you've been there</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1634.87,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 8:19-22 - Creation waits and groans","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Compare life's sufferings - Romans <b>thrown out of homes for a year</b> when emperor angry at Jews, persecuted</li><li class=\"d1\">\"legit suffering,\" not \"dropped my Starbucks\" - still <b>nothing</b> next to the destiny</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verse 19</b>: creation eagerly waits for the <b>revealing of the sons of God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">whole creation waits for Christ's return: purified, transformed - world, animals, plants</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Genesis 3</b>: \"cursed is the ground because of you\"</li><li class=\"d1\">humans given <b>dominion</b> → our sin <b>destructive to the whole creation</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verse 20</b>: subjected to <b>futility</b> in Genesis 3, not willingly, \"in hope\"</li><li class=\"d1\">hope: humans given mortal flesh so they could <b>repent and be restored</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verse 21</b>: creation delivered from <b>bondage of corruption</b> into the liberty of God's children</li><li class=\"d1\">freed from the leftover <b>taint of our sin</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verse 22</b>: whole creation groans, labors with <b>birth pangs</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1784.37,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 8:23-25 - First fruits and hope","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verse 23</b>: we have the <b>first fruits</b> of the Spirit, groan, wait for adoption, <b>redemption of our body</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>First fruits</b> = first growth of planted crops</li><li class=\"d1\">guarantee: crop is coming, didn't die in winter freeze</li><li class=\"d0\">The Spirit = <b>beginning of our transformation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">walking after the Spirit now = beginning of path to destiny; <b>guarantee</b> received</li><li class=\"d0\">Body (not flesh) redeemed when Christ returns, world restored</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verse 24</b>: saved in hope - hope seen is not hope</li><li class=\"d1\">saved from power of sin and death <b>for this hope</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"I'm not going to hell, now do whatever, try not to sin too much\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>free now to follow the Spirit</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Don't hope for what you have - Amazon package in hand</li><li class=\"d1\">destiny not achieved yet → wait with <b>perseverance</b> (v.25)</li></ul>"},{"t":1905.18,"lv":2,"h":"Romans 8:26-27 - The Spirit intercedes","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Verses 26-27</b>: Spirit helps our weakness; we <b>don't know what to pray for</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Spirit intercedes with <b>groanings which cannot be uttered</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the One who searches hearts knows the mind of the Spirit; intercedes <b>according to God's will</b></li><li class=\"d0\">We pray for things of the <b>mind of the flesh</b></li><li class=\"d1\">promotion, pass a test I didn't study for, win the lottery</li><li class=\"d0\">Health: pray quickly when sick; <b>rarely thank God when healthy</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Spirit knows his own mind - contrast of mind of flesh / mind of Spirit</li><li class=\"d1\">image: Holy Spirit <b>translates</b> to the Father what we say into what we <b>really need</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2003.6,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: praying for the fruits of the Spirit","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Comment: Coptic pope <b>Shenouda</b> (passed away) - we should pray for the <b>fruits of the Spirit</b>: meekness, love, joy</li><li class=\"d1\">persevere and you're guaranteed to get them; wisdom too</li><li class=\"d0\">Fr S: Christ: don't worry what you'll eat or wear - <b>seek first the kingdom</b>, the rest taken care of</li><li class=\"d0\">James: if anyone lacks wisdom, <b>ask God</b>, who gives generously</li><li class=\"d0\">Even asking for wrong things → Spirit translates to what we actually need</li><li class=\"d0\">Protestant days: \"don't pray for <b>patience</b> - you'll get it\"</li><li class=\"d1\">tested again and again until you get it</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Augustine</b>: \"Lord, give me chastity, but not yet\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Good place to leave off, though not end of chapter</li><li class=\"d1\">next: <b>predestination</b> - \"requires its own discussion\"</li></ul>"}],"next":"Next: <b>Romans 8:28</b> onward - predestination"});
